<article class="env-lemma" id="05SN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05SN">Lemma <span data-tag="05SN">12.19.11</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $A, B, C \in \text{Fil}(\mathcal{A})$. Let $f : B \to A$ and $g : C \to A$ be morphisms. Then there exists a fibre product </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ B \times _ A C \ar[r]_{g'} \ar[d]_{f'} &  B \ar[d]^ f \\  C \ar[r]^ g &  A }  \]
</div>
  <p> in $\text{Fil}(\mathcal{A})$. If $f$ is strict, so is $f'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This lemma is dual to Lemma <a href="/tag/05SM" data-tag="05SM">12.19.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>